  data: {
    LLM: "Assess Your Hand. If you have many high cards (Aces/Kings), use them in your Positive (Trump) rounds to rack up +50s. If you have low cards or a 'Void' in a suit, choose 'Rıfkı' or 'Girls'. The most important rule is: DON'T LEAD Rıfkı (King of Hearts) unless you have toâ€”once it is out, the tension of that round vanishes.\n\nContract Exhaustion: Keep track of which negative contracts haven't been played yet. If 'Last Two' is still available and you have low cards, wait for someone else to lead a high-card round. Also, if you know an opponent is desperate to play a positive round, 'Trump' their high cards as early as possible to minimize their gain.\n\nThe 'Rıfkı' Trap: In the Rıfkı round, if you hold the Queen or Jack of Hearts, you are in a power position. You can 'Flush Out' the King of Hearts from whoever holds it by leading small hearts. If *you* hold the King of Hearts, try to play it on an opponent's Ace lead as quickly as possible to get rid of the -320 penalty early.",
    Player: "Assess Your Hand. If you have many high cards (Aces/Kings), use them in your Positive (Trump) rounds to rack up +50s. If you have low cards or a 'Void' in a suit, choose 'Rıfkı' or 'Girls'. The most important rule is: DON'T LEAD Rıfkı (King of Hearts) unless you have toâ€”once it is out, the tension of that round vanishes.\n\nContract Exhaustion: Keep track of which negative contracts haven't been played yet. If 'Last Two' is still available and you have low cards, wait for someone else to lead a high-card round. Also, if you know an opponent is desperate to play a positive round, 'Trump' their high cards as early as possible to minimize their gain.\n\nThe 'Rıfkı' Trap: In the Rıfkı round, if you hold the Queen or Jack of Hearts, you are in a power position. You can 'Flush Out' the King of Hearts from whoever holds it by leading small hearts. If *you* hold the King of Hearts, try to play it on an opponent's Ace lead as quickly as possible to get rid of the -320 penalty early.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
    bluffFrequency: 0.3,
    bluffSettings: {
      profile: 'balanced',
